{
  "version": 2,
  "shape": "build-up",
  "tone": "energy",
  "story": {
    "hero": "home",
    "logline": "Your roof catches sun all day; power you use yourself saves far more than power you sell, so how soon does solar pay you back?"
  },
  "question": "Should I put solar on my roof?",
  "source": {
    "title": "Homeowner's Guide to Solar; Will I Save Money with Solar Energy?",
    "publisher": "U.S. Department of Energy, U.S. EIA, EnergySage, CPUC",
    "url": "https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar/homeowners-guide-going-solar",
    "quotes": [
      "Typically, solar panels perform best on south-facing roofs with a slope between 15 and 40 degrees, though other roofs may be suitable too.",
      "Your savings also depend on the electricity rates set by your utility and how much the utility will compensate you for the excess solar energy you send back to the grid.",
      "Net metering is an arrangement between solar energy system owners and utilities in which the system owners are compensated for any solar power generation that is exported to the electricity grid.",
      "In general, a purchased solar system can be installed at a lower total cost than system installed using a solar loan, lease, or power purchase agreement (PPA).",
      "If you pay cash for your solar system, the payback period refers to the length of time required before the system has paid for itself and all future power produced is free.",
      "You should also consider the age of your roof and how long until it will need replacement.",
      "Every household is different... so calculating an average amount of savings from going solar is nearly impossible.",
      {
        "text": "The average U.S. residential electricity price rose from 16.0 cents per kilowatthour (kWh) in 2023 to 16.5 cents/kWh in 2024",
        "url": "https://www.eia.gov/todayinenergy/detail.php?id=65244",
        "publisher": "U.S. EIA",
        "accessed": "2026-11-05"
      },
      {
        "text": "The average electric monthly bill for U.S. residential customers was $144 in 2024",
        "url": "https://www.eia.gov/todayinenergy/detail.php?id=65244",
        "publisher": "U.S. EIA",
        "accessed": "2026-11-05"
      },
      {
        "text": "Right now, systems average about $2.60 per watt before incentives.",
        "url": "https://www.energysage.com/local-data/solar-panel-cost/",
        "publisher": "EnergySage",
        "accessed": "2026-11-05"
      },
      {
        "text": "Solar batteries typically cost $15,647 before any available incentives",
        "url": "https://www.energysage.com/local-data/energy-storage-cost/",
        "publisher": "EnergySage",
        "accessed": "2026-11-05"
      },
      {
        "text": "Solar to Battery to Home/Grid Round Trip Efficiency: 89%",
        "url": "https://energylibrary.tesla.com/docs/Public/EnergyStorage/Powerwall/3/InstallManual/BackupSwitch/en-us/GUID-EC527BC7-4750-4425-BBC4-DB8C000339B3.html",
        "publisher": "Tesla Powerwall 3 manual",
        "accessed": "2026-11-05"
      },
      {
        "text": "Export compensation is usually lower than the retail rate.",
        "url": "https://www.cpuc.ca.gov/industries-and-topics/electrical-energy/demand-side-management/customer-generation/net-energy-metering-and-net-billing",
        "publisher": "California Public Utilities Commission",
        "accessed": "2026-11-05"
      },
      {
        "text": "Installed cost per watt by state: AZ $2.25, CA $2.52, TX $2.25, FL $2.12, NY $2.77.",
        "url": "https://www.energysage.com/local-data/solar-panel-cost/",
        "publisher": "EnergySage (table)",
        "accessed": "2026-11-05"
      },
      {
        "text": "Peak sun hours per day by state: AZ 6.5, CA 5.82, TX 5.64, FL 5.44, NY 3.58.",
        "url": "https://www.energysage.com/solar/many-sunlight-hours-need-calculating-peak-sun-hours/",
        "publisher": "EnergySage (table)",
        "accessed": "2026-11-05"
      },
      {
        "text": "Average residential price, August 2026, cents/kWh: AZ 15.05, CA 29.75, TX 15.91, FL 14.99, NY 28.65.",
        "url": "https://www.eia.gov/electricity/monthly/epm_table_grapher.php?t=epmt_5_6_a",
        "publisher": "U.S. EIA, Electric Power Monthly Table 5.6.A",
        "accessed": "2026-11-05"
      }
    ]
  },
  "model": {
    "inputs": [
      {
        "id": "size",
        "label": "System size",
        "unit": "kW",
        "kind": "lever",
        "min": 2,
        "max": 12,
        "step": 0.5,
        "default": 7,
        "source": "assumption"
      },
      {
        "id": "battery",
        "label": "Home battery",
        "unit": "kWh",
        "kind": "lever",
        "min": 0,
        "max": 20,
        "step": 1,
        "default": 0,
        "source": "assumption"
      },
      {
        "id": "selfUse",
        "label": "Solar used as it's made",
        "unit": "%",
        "kind": "lever",
        "min": 20,
        "max": 80,
        "step": 5,
        "default": 40,
        "source": "assumption"
      },
      {
        "id": "monthlyBill",
        "label": "Your monthly power bill",
        "unit": "$/month",
        "kind": "condition",
        "min": 40,
        "max": 500,
        "step": 5,
        "default": 145,
        "source": "article",
        "quote": 8
      },
      {
        "id": "price",
        "label": "Price you pay for power",
        "unit": "$/kWh",
        "kind": "condition",
        "min": 0.1,
        "max": 0.45,
        "step": 0.01,
        "default": 0.165,
        "source": "article",
        "quote": 7
      },
      {
        "id": "exportRate",
        "label": "Credit for power you send out",
        "unit": "$/kWh",
        "kind": "condition",
        "min": 0,
        "max": 0.3,
        "step": 0.01,
        "default": 0.05,
        "source": "assumption"
      },
      {
        "id": "costPerKw",
        "label": "Installed cost per kW",
        "unit": "$/kW",
        "kind": "condition",
        "min": 1800,
        "max": 4500,
        "step": 50,
        "default": 2600,
        "source": "article",
        "quote": 9
      },
      {
        "id": "sunHours",
        "label": "Full-sun hours a day",
        "unit": "h/day",
        "kind": "condition",
        "min": 3,
        "max": 6.5,
        "step": 0.1,
        "default": 4.5,
        "source": "assumption"
      }
    ],
    "constants": [
      {
        "id": "efficiency",
        "label": "Share of panel output that reaches your home",
        "unit": "",
        "value": 0.8,
        "source": "assumption"
      },
      {
        "id": "roundTrip",
        "label": "Power a battery gives back",
        "unit": "",
        "value": 0.89,
        "source": "article",
        "quote": 11
      },
      {
        "id": "batteryCost",
        "label": "Installed battery cost per kWh (about $15,600 for 13.5 kWh)",
        "unit": "$/kWh",
        "value": 1150,
        "source": "assumption"
      },
      {
        "id": "cycles",
        "label": "Times the battery fills and empties a day",
        "unit": "/day",
        "value": 1,
        "source": "assumption"
      }
    ],
    "derived": [
      {
        "id": "useKwh",
        "label": "Power your home uses a year",
        "unit": "kWh/yr",
        "formula": "monthlyBill * 12 / price"
      },
      {
        "id": "yearlyKwh",
        "label": "Power the panels make a year",
        "unit": "kWh/yr",
        "formula": "size * sunHours * 365 * efficiency"
      },
      {
        "id": "direct",
        "label": "Used as it's made",
        "unit": "kWh/yr",
        "formula": "min(yearlyKwh * selfUse / 100, useKwh)"
      },
      {
        "id": "surplus",
        "label": "Not used right away",
        "unit": "kWh/yr",
        "formula": "yearlyKwh - direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "shifted",
        "label": "Stored and used later",
        "unit": "kWh/yr",
        "formula": "min(surplus * roundTrip, battery * cycles * 365, useKwh - direct)"
      },
      {
        "id": "exportedKwh",
        "label": "Sent to the grid",
        "unit": "kWh/yr",
        "formula": "surplus - shifted / roundTrip"
      },
      {
        "id": "boughtKwh",
        "label": "Still bought from the grid",
        "unit": "kWh/yr",
        "formula": "useKwh - direct - shifted"
      },
      {
        "id": "billSaving",
        "label": "Bill you avoid",
        "unit": "$/yr",
        "formula": "(direct + shifted) * price"
      },
      {
        "id": "exportCredit",
        "label": "Export credit",
        "unit": "$/yr",
        "formula": "exportedKwh * exportRate"
      },
      {
        "id": "cost",
        "label": "System cost",
        "unit": "$",
        "formula": "size * costPerKw + battery * batteryCost"
      }
    ],
    "outputs": [
      {
        "id": "saving",
        "label": "Saved each year",
        "unit": "$/yr",
        "formula": "billSaving + exportCredit"
      },
      {
        "id": "newBill",
        "label": "Your monthly bill after",
        "unit": "$/month",
        "formula": "max(boughtKwh * price - exportCredit, 0) / 12"
      }
    ],
    "stores": [
      {
        "id": "savings",
        "label": "Savings so far",
        "unit": "$",
        "start": 0,
        "change": "saving"
      }
    ],
    "milestones": [
      {
        "id": "paidBack",
        "label": "Paid back in",
        "store": "savings",
        "reaches": "cost"
      }
    ]
  },
  "world": {
    "time": {
      "unit": "year",
      "span": 25
    },
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "sun",
        "prop": "sun",
        "label": "Sun",
        "plays": "sunHours",
        "sky": true
      },
      {
        "id": "home",
        "prop": "house",
        "label": "Your home",
        "plays": "selfUse"
      },
      {
        "id": "panels",
        "prop": "roof-panel",
        "label": "Panels",
        "plays": "size",
        "on": "home"
      },
      {
        "id": "bat",
        "prop": "battery",
        "label": "Home battery",
        "plays": "battery",
        "appears": "battery"
      },
      {
        "id": "grid",
        "prop": "power-pole",
        "label": "The grid",
        "plays": "exportRate"
      },
      {
        "id": "jar",
        "prop": "jar",
        "label": "Savings",
        "store": "savings",
        "target": "cost"
      }
    ],
    "flows": [
      {
        "id": "light",
        "from": "sun",
        "to": "panels",
        "carrier": "light",
        "rate": "sunHours",
        "label": "Sunlight",
        "unit": "h/day"
      },
      {
        "id": "direct",
        "from": "panels",
        "to": "home",
        "carrier": "energy",
        "rate": "direct",
        "label": "Used as it's made",
        "unit": "kWh/yr"
      },
      {
        "id": "charge",
        "from": "panels",
        "to": "bat",
        "carrier": "energy",
        "rate": "shifted / roundTrip",
        "label": "Stored for later",
        "unit": "kWh/yr"
      },
      {
        "id": "discharge",
        "from": "bat",
        "to": "home",
        "carrier": "energy",
        "rate": "shifted",
        "label": "Used in the evening",
        "unit": "kWh/yr"
      },
      {
        "id": "export",
        "from": "panels",
        "to": "grid",
        "carrier": "energy",
        "rate": "exportedKwh",
        "label": "Sent to the grid",
        "unit": "kWh/yr"
      },
      {
        "id": "import",
        "from": "grid",
        "to": "home",
        "carrier": "energy",
        "rate": "boughtKwh",
        "label": "Bought from the grid",
        "unit": "kWh/yr"
      },
      {
        "id": "avoided",
        "from": "home",
        "to": "jar",
        "carrier": "money",
        "rate": "billSaving",
        "label": "Bill you avoid",
        "unit": "$/yr"
      },
      {
        "id": "credit",
        "from": "grid",
        "to": "jar",
        "carrier": "money",
        "rate": "exportCredit",
        "label": "What the grid pays you",
        "unit": "$/yr"
      }
    ]
  },
  "ask": [
    {
      "question": "What is your average monthly power bill?",
      "help": "Add up your last few bills and divide by how many.",
      "input": "monthlyBill"
    },
    {
      "question": "Where do you live?",
      "help": "Sets typical sun, power price and install cost. Somewhere else uses typical US values. You can change each one later.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "Arizona",
          "set": {
            "sunHours": 6.5,
            "price": 0.15,
            "costPerKw": 2250
          },
          "quote": [
            13,
            14,
            15
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "California",
          "set": {
            "sunHours": 5.8,
            "price": 0.3,
            "costPerKw": 2520
          },
          "quote": [
            13,
            14,
            15
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Texas",
          "set": {
            "sunHours": 5.6,
            "price": 0.16,
            "costPerKw": 2250
          },
          "quote": [
            13,
            14,
            15
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "New York",
          "set": {
            "sunHours": 3.6,
            "price": 0.29,
            "costPerKw": 2770
          },
          "quote": [
            13,
            14,
            15
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Somewhere else",
